  <h1>Network Troubleshooting Commands Every IT Support Engineer Should Know</h1>

  <p>
    Network troubleshooting is an essential skill for IT Support Engineers.
    Learn how to diagnose connectivity, IP configuration, DNS and routing issues.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Ping Command</h2>
  <p>Test connectivity to another device or server.</p>
  <pre><code>ping 8.8.8.8</code></pre>

  <h2>2. IP Configuration</h2>
  <p>Check the IP address and default gateway on Windows.</p>
  <pre><code>ipconfig /all</code></pre>

  <h2>3. Trace Network Route</h2>
  <pre><code>tracert google.com</code></pre>

  <h2>4. DNS Lookup</h2>
  <pre><code>nslookup google.com</code></pre>

  <h2>5. Network Connections</h2>
  <pre><code>netstat -ano</code></pre>

